From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 03:12:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 163/169] Kernel preparation: TileLang MoE experts and mHC
 declare, bind and warm

The routed experts' plan lists its grouped GEMMs, TileKernels' fused SwiGLU
(whose factory our code calls with every key) and both dispatch plans' dispatch,
combine and fold kernels as calls, binds them once prepared, and warms
TileKernels' MXFP8 token cast for each batch bucket. Weight processing keeps the
tile-major repack; the layer's MoE method lets its modular experts declare.

TileKernelsMHC declares project_streams for each entry mode (and the
unreduced post_pre of the TP world under SP) and both finalize widths, binds
the forward's cached kernels, and warms TileKernels' post and stream collapse
on one zero token.
